.page-section.p-120-cont.cg-section.grey-light-bg.clearfix(id="ai-link")
    .container
        .row
            .col-md-10.col-md-offset-1.text-center.mb-60
                h2.cg-section-title AI that ships inside real systems
                p.cg-section-lead We use AI-assisted development to move faster on audits, refactors, and migrations—and we integrate AI capabilities into the backends you already run on AWS.
        .row
            .col-md-6
                .cg-outcome-card.wow.fadeIn
                    h3 AI-assisted engineering (how we work)
                    p Senior engineers stay in charge of architecture and production risk. AI accelerates the work around them:
                    ul.cg-bullet-list
                        li Faster codebase reconnaissance across Go services, Lambdas, and IaC
                        li Assisted profiling notes, test scaffolding, and migration diffs—reviewed before merge
                        li Shorter cycles from diagnosis to a deployable change set your team can own
            .col-md-6
                .cg-outcome-card.wow.fadeIn(data-wow-delay='150ms')
                    h3 AI integration into your stack
                    p When you need AI features in production, we wire them into existing systems—not a disconnected demo:
                    ul.cg-bullet-list
                        li LLM and inference paths on AWS (Bedrock, Lambda, queues, API Gateway)
                        li Event-driven pipelines that call models without blocking core APIs
                        li Cost, latency, and reliability controls so AI workloads do not surprise the bill or the SLO
        .row
            .col-md-10.col-md-offset-1.text-center.mt-20
                p.cg-section-lead Same standard as the rest of our practice: production-safe design, measurable outcomes, and handoff your platform team can operate.
